# Descriptor for this agent. agent-mgr supplies everything else.
#
# Every key here is optional -- agent-mgr derives all of them from the agent's
# name. Set one only to override the convention, and say why.
#
#   AGENT_HOME       default ~/.hermes-<name>
#   AGENT_CONTAINER  default hermes-<name>
#   AGENT_PROJECT    default hermes-<name>
#   AGENT_TZ         default America/Los_Angeles -- but NOT here if more
#                    than one instance is registered against this repo:
#                    every one reads this file, so a zone set here is
#                    given to all of them. Per-instance values go in
#                    ~/.config/agent-mgr/<name>.env
#   AGENT_IMAGE      default the digest in agent-mgr's runtime/image.ref
#   AGENT_CONFIG     default config.yaml, resolved against this directory
#
# Two more, optional and unset by default. Both are paths in this repo,
# resolved against this directory, and both must be executable:
#
#   AGENT_RESTORE_HOOK      a script `agent-mgr restore` runs after its own
#                           installs -- this agent's own restore step, such as
#                           seeding a corpus. Sequenced by agent-mgr so that one
#                           command is the whole deploy. A non-zero exit fails
#                           the restore.
#
#   AGENT_PRE_TRANSITION    this agent's veto on stopping or replacing its
#                           container. Every route to a transition goes through
#                           one seam, so it is asked before all of them -- the
#                           reload that follows a write included -- and a
#                           non-zero exit refuses. Use it for work that must not
#                           be interrupted; the rentals agent checks for an
#                           in-flight ingest.
#
#                           Two things to know when writing one. `activate` is
#                           the one command a refusal does NOT fail: it has
#                           already spent a one-time activation by then, so it
#                           reports success and skips the restart rather than
#                           inviting you to spend another. And `restore` asks
#                           twice -- once as a preflight before it writes
#                           anything, again at the reload it ends with -- so
#                           write the guard to be safe to ask more than once.
#
# Both receive this descriptor's non-AGENT_ variables in their environment.
#
# An instance that needs a derived image or extra mounts adds a
# compose.override.yml beside this file and sets the variables it names here.
